WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.239
In Moscow

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:06.873
today, a court

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.108
ordered the arrest of well-known

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.142
investigative journalist

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.077
Christo grows up and grows out of

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:11.611
who works with.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.346
Bellingcat has an extensive track

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.948
record of uncovering stories

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.082
exposing the Kremlin.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.484
And Vladimir Putin

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:18.351
herself was a key

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.652
figure in investigating the plot.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.987
To kill Russian opposition leader

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.355
Alexei Navalny and has been on

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.424
Russia's most wanted list since December.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:28.061
He joins me for an exclusive interview

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.696
Christo, thank you very much

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.597
for being with us.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:31.798
To the best of your understanding,

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.900
why did Russia order your arrest?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.302
What reason did they give?

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.737
Well, the mystery began

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.671
about four months ago

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.206
when I was put on the international

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.441
wanted list by Russia.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.044
And they had absolutely no information

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:44.911
put out there.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.745
Why they're looking for

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.513
me around the world.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.848
It just said for breaking the law.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:49.883
And today,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.018
during the arrest hearings in Moscow,

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.153
I found out for the first time

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.054
that actually the reason

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.789
why they have been looking for me

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.357
or want to arrest me and are inviting me

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.159
is because apparently in their views,

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.494
I organized the escape from Russia

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.562
of a persecuted

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.230
Russian called a Russian journalist

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.698
from the of whom

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.933
they raided

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.102
the house of his parents house.

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.204
And he left Russia

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.138
in the middle of the night

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.374
one Friday, about a couple of years ago.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:15.642
So they are saying that

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.776
I organized all of that.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.112
And if that's the charge that I

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:20.747
have to live with, then

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.482
I could be happier.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:25.952
Is that something you were involved with?

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.420
Well, let's leave it at

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.922
that, that I would gladly help

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.390
any help any Russian

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.691
journalist get out of the country

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.225
if they are

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.527
if they feel prosecuted or persecuted.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.628
There had been this report

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.198
and that Russian investigators had

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.032
told the court

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.501
an illegal crossing of

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:42.936
the border of the Russian Federation.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.438
That's what that was in reference to.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:45.905
Correct.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.140
There was some misunderstanding

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.274
by colleagues, by media

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.275
who thought they had crossed

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.043
the border illegally.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.411
I would never dare do that.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.378
I mean, I've been blacklisted

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.380
by Russia since 2006.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.015
Never crossed into it.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.118
But but yeah, it's a colleague

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.919
who crossed the border without a passport

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:00.920
because they had four feet

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.021
of this passport

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.323
a couple of hours earlier.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.525
And I'm kind of the conspirator

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.860
or the organizer of that event

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.994
in their eyes.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.230
In terms of your reporting.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:10.964
I mean, obviously,

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.866
you have been in the forefront

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.135
of some extraordinary work.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:15.902
Do you believe there's

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.004
a particular piece of your reporting

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.239
that Russian authorities

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.708
have been been singling you out for?

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.310
Anderson, take your pick.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.813
I mean, I've covered the shoot down

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.614
by Malaysia,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:28.414
by Russian

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:32.118
air forces of Malaysian airliner, MH 17.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.720
I've covered the Skripal poisoning,

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.723
the explosions around Munich in Europe,

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:37.891
the Navalny pausing.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.826
I think the Navalny poisoning was one

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.895
that was particularly painful

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.229
for the Russian FSB,

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.331
for the security machine, because it

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.900
not only disclosed that they did it,

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.901
but put them in a very,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.869
very, let's say, unflattering

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.171
light of bumbling idiot.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:51.871
So I would

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:52.472
I would take

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.175
that as my book has being on

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.409
Russia's wanted list.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.478
Has it affected your life?

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.579
I mean, obviously,

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.014
you have to take

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.483
that kind of thing very seriously.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.852
Well, clearly, I cannot travel to

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.519
certain countries

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.053
that previously

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:07.787
I would have traveled

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.088
to for investigations

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.724
and for journalistic purposes.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:12.692
I have to think twice

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.260
before leaving the country

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.962
I am in the moment.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.397
But I would say that

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.998
that's not the scariest thing out there,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.266
because being on the wanted

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.634
list is one thing.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:25.471
Russia always delves into sort of

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:26.973
lanes.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.542
They have the judicial

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.344
sort of pursuit and persecution,

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:32.845
and then they have the extrajudicial

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.846
one and

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.448
today, by the way, in addition to me

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.916
being put on the on

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.384
being arrested virtually,

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.352
which is the crazy

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.653
Russian invention

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.689
arrest in absentia, I was also put on the

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:43.723
what they call

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.891
the foreign agent list

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.292
for the first time,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.161
which is strange because I'm a foreigner.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.096
So I obviously

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.297
belong on a foreign agent list

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.365
because otherwise you should be

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.566
there as well.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.135
But together with me, a couple of Russian

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.237
journalists were put on the list,

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:59.172
including a very brave

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.008
young lady who was poisoned

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.076
in the last few months.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.445
By the same machine, repressive machine.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.180
So that's that

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.214
just gives you an indication

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.383
that being pursued

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.551
within the

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.619
confines of the law

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.587
is not the scariest thing.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:14.821
Yeah.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.190
I mean, obviously, we have seen

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.993
people poisoned in in foreign countries

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:23.062
by Russian by Russian agents.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.064
That's got to be something.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.065
I mean, you are

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.300
obviously very aware of it's

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:27.867
got to be something

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:30.270
that I mean, does it change the way you

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.906
operate on a daily basis?

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.440
Definitely.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.309
I mean, you do have to think twice before

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:37.410
touching a door handle

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.213
and then accepting tea from a stranger

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.347
or water from a stranger

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:41.714
that may

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.516
have to become your second nature.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.785
And all of my colleagues at Bellingcat

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.953
have kind of

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.321
had to learn to live

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.456
with this new escalated risk,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.892
as many Russian colleagues of ours

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.460
have done for years.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.061
Crystal Groves,

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.562
I appreciate your time tonight.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.231
Thank you very much.

